    "content": "(Word Count: 482 words / Limit: 500 words)\n\nSystem Architecture Overview\nMatriDrishti is architected as an enterprise, resilient, offline-first microservices platform designed for sovereign containerized deployment on Kubernetes within the Assam State Data Centre (ASDC). The platform strictly adheres to the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM) standards, leveraging M1, M2, and M3 milestones (ABHA creation, Health Facility Registry [HFR], and FHIR-compliant Electronic Health Records).\n\n`\n[ Frontline Layer: BLE Cuffs & Optical OCR ]\n              \u2502\n              \u25bc\n[ Offline-First Edge App (WatermelonDB / SQLite) ] \u25c4\u2500\u2500 (Zero-Connectivity in Chars/Tea Belts)\n              \u2502\n     (Encrypted TLS 1.3 Sync via ABDM Gateway)\n              \u2502\n              \u25bc\n[ ASDC Cloud Gateway (Kong / Envoy + Redis 7.2) ]\n              \u2502\n     \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n     \u25bc                                 \u25bc                      \u25bc\n[ Clinical CDSS Engine ]    [ AI Risk ML Pipeline ]   [ Emergency Referral Hub ]\n(GoI/WHO Clinical Rules)    (Longitudinal MAP XGBoost) (108 Mrityunjoy / FRU Bed)\n     \u2502                                 \u2502                      \u2502\n     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n              \u25bc\n[ State Health Command & Multi-Tenant Data Store ]\n(PostgreSQL 16 + PostGIS + TimescaleDB Timeseries + MinIO Vault)\n`\n\nCore Architectural Layers & Enterprise Technology Stack\n\n1. Frontline Edge & Telemetry Layer:\n\u2022 Mobile Client: React Native / TypeScript with WatermelonDB (SQLite reactive storage engine), achieving 60 FPS fluidity on low-cost Android Go (2GB RAM) smartphones distributed under NHM and Poshan Abhiyaan.\n\u2022 IoT Telemetry Interface: Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) GATT profile communication with CDSCO/FDA-approved blood pressure cuffs adhering to the IEEE 11073-10407 health device communication standard.\n\u2022 Edge Computer Vision: On-device TensorFlow Lite OCR and OpenCV colorimetry models running locally at 30 FPS to parse digits from analog dials/older LCDs and grade urine dipstick strips without cloud dependency.\n\n2. ASDC Microservices & Data Core:\n\u2022 API Gateway & Auth: Kong Gateway, OpenID Connect / OAuth2, and strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) separating ASHA, ANM, Medical Officer, and State Admin roles.\n\u2022 Primary Relational & Geospatial Database: PostgreSQL 16 with PostGIS 3.4 for facility catchment polygons, village boundary mapping, and road network routing.\n\u2022 Clinical Timeseries Storage: TimescaleDB hypertable engine indexing high-frequency longitudinal vitals (MAP, SBP, DBP, Heart Rate, Proteinuria, Gestational Age).\n\u2022 Message Broker & In-Memory Cache: Apache Kafka for asynchronous processing of incoming screening events, referral triggers, and broadcast queues; Redis 7.2 cluster for sub-millisecond session caching.\n\n3. AI & Clinical Risk Engine:\n\u2022 Risk Modeling Framework: Python 3.11, Scikit-learn, XGBoost, and PyTorch Lightning. Models are trained on multi-centric maternal cohorts, utilizing SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) to provide explainable risk factors to attending doctors.\n\u2022 Clinical Decision Rules: Drools / JsonLogic rule engine executing validated GoI National Health Guidelines for High-Risk Pregnancies.\n\n4. Security, Privacy & Interoperability:\n\u2022 Data Protection: Full compliance with India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023 and DISHA guidelines. AES-256 encryption at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit, and irreversible cryptographic hashing of maternal identifiable information.\n\u2022 ABDM & FHIR: Native support for HL7 FHIR R4 resources (Observation, Condition, Encounter, CarePlan), seamless ABHA number linkage, and two-way e-Kavach interoperability."
