    "content": "(Word Count: 468 words / Limit: 500 words)\n\nAgile Clinical Spiral Development Methodology\nMatriDrishti follows an Agile Clinical Spiral Framework combining rapid software engineering sprints with rigorous clinical co-design and validation alongside Assam\u2019s premier medical institutions. The development lifecycle spans five sequential, interdependent phases:\n\n`\n[ Phase 1: Clinical Co-Design & Protocol Formulation (M1-M2) ]\n                             \u2502\n                             \u25bc\n[ Phase 2: Hardware Telemetry & Edge Firmware Prototyping (M3) ]\n                             \u2502\n                             \u25bc\n[ Phase 3: Alpha Testing, Synthetic Simulation & Benchmarking (M4-M5) ]\n                             \u2502\n                             \u25bc\n[ Phase 4: Field MVP Pilot in Tea Gardens & Riverine Chars (M6-M8) ]\n                             \u2502\n                             \u25bc\n[ Phase 5: Statewide Hardening, Emergency Integration & Handover (M9-M12) ]\n`\n\nDetailed Intermediate Steps & Key Deliverables\n\n1. Discovery, Clinical Co-Design & Protocol Digitization (Months 1\u20132):\n\u2022 Convene a Joint Clinical Advisory Committee with Obstetric and Community Medicine faculties from Assam Medical College Hospital (AMCH), Dibrugarh, and Gauhati Medical College Hospital (GMCH).\n\u2022 Digitize Government of India High-Risk Pregnancy guidelines, standardizing algorithmic rules for prophylactic Low-Dose Aspirin (75\u2013150 mg before 16 weeks), elemental calcium, and Pritchard \\text{MgSO}_4 emergency administration.\n\u2022 Key Output: Frozen Clinical Logic Specification & Ethics Board Review Dossier.\n\n2. Hardware Telemetry & Edge Firmware Prototyping (Month 3):\n\u2022 Develop custom BLE GATT communication profiles for CDSCO-approved wireless BP monitors (Omron/Sunbeam) under IEEE 11073-10407 standards.\n\u2022 Train on-device TensorFlow Lite computer vision models for optical dial/LCD character recognition and 4-tier colorimetric dipstick grading.\n\u2022 Key Output: Functional Edge Telemetry SDK and Bilingual ASHA Wireframe Prototype.\n\n3. Alpha Testing, Synthetic Simulation & Lab Benchmarking (Months 4\u20135):\n\u2022 Provision secure containerized staging environments within the Assam State Data Centre (ASDC).\n\u2022 Generate synthetic longitudinal maternal cohorts (10,000 simulated pregnancies) matching Assam\u2019s demographic, parity, and hemodynamic profiles.\n\u2022 Conduct chaos-engineering resilience testing: simulate complete network blackouts, queuing 5,000 offline screening encounters in local SQLite/WatermelonDB storage and verifying zero-loss reconciliation upon simulated 2G reconnect.\n\u2022 Key Output: ASDC Staging Deployment, Tested ML Pipeline (AUC > 0.93), and VAPT Security Report.\n\n4. Field MVP Pilot & Rapid Feedback Loop (Months 6\u20138):\n\u2022 Procure and deploy 600 BLE BP kits across two contrasting high-vulnerability testbeds: Dibrugarh (40 tea estate hospitals) and Barpeta (35 riverine char Sub-Centres).\n\u2022 Conduct hands-on training for 500 ASHA workers and 120 ANMs using high-contrast, iconographic bilingual interfaces.\n\u2022 Establish live prospective monitoring of 6,000 pregnant women, capturing real-world device pairing telemetry and user friction points.\n\u2022 Key Output: Calibrated Field MVP, Mid-Term Clinical Validation Report, and ASHA Usability Scorecard.\n\n5. Statewide Hardening, Emergency Integration & Institutional Handover (Months 9\u201312):\n\u2022 Integrate automated referral dispatch webhooks with GVK EMRI 108/102 Mrityunjoy CAD systems and First Referral Unit (FRU) obstetric ICU bed tracking.\n\u2022 Execute bidirectional ABDM FHIR R4 bridge linking MatriDrishti with national e-Kavach and the RCH portal.\n\u2022 Deliver comprehensive system source code, administrative cryptographic keys, and operational runbooks to the NHM Assam State IT Cell.\n\u2022 Key Output: Certified Production Release, CERT-In Audit Clearance, and Final Handover Charter."
