    "content": "(Word Count: 462 words / Limit: 500 words)\n\n12-Month Phased Roadmap & Key Milestones\nThe project is structured into four sequential 3-month phases with clear validation gates, deliverables, and risk mitigation checkpoints to ensure flawless transition from lab prototyping to statewide institutionalization:\n\n`\nMonth:  M01 M02 M03 \u2502 M04 M05 M06 \u2502 M07 M08 M09 \u2502 M10 M11 M12\nPhase:  [ Phase 1 ] \u2502 [ Phase 2 ] \u2502 [ Phase 3 ] \u2502 [ Phase 4 ]\nGate:               \u25b2             \u25b2             \u25b2             \u25b2\n                 ASDC Core    Pilot Gate    Scale Gate    NHM Handover\n`\n\nPhase-Wise Deliverables, Dependencies & Validation Gates\n\n\u2022 Phase 1: Clinical Co-Design, Edge Telemetry & ASDC Cloud Foundation (Months 1\u20133)\n\u2022 M1: Form Clinical Advisory Committee with AMCH Dibrugarh and GMCH; establish liaison with NHM Assam. Digitize GoI clinical rules.\n\u2022 M2: Provision sovereign Kubernetes, PostgreSQL 16, TimescaleDB, and Redis 7.2 instances at Assam State Data Centre (ASDC). Build BLE GATT drivers.\n\u2022 M3: Develop offline React Native client with WatermelonDB/SQLite and on-device OpenCV/TensorFlow Lite OCR.\n\u2022 Deliverables: Clinical Logic Specification, ASDC Staging Environment, Edge Telemetry Prototype.\n\u2022 Dependencies: ASDC virtual server allocation, institutional ethics approvals from AMCH/GMCH.\n\n\u2022 Phase 2: High-Vulnerability Field Pilot & Mid-Term Clinical Validation (Months 4\u20136)\n\u2022 M4: Procure 600 CDSCO-approved BLE BP monitors and 10,000 dipstick kits. Stage bilingual (Assamese/English) client.\n\u2022 M5: Conduct master training for 500 ASHAs and 120 ANMs across Dibrugarh (tea gardens) and Barpeta (char Sub-Centres).\n\u2022 M6: Launch live screening cohort of 6,000 expectant mothers. Calibrate MAP trajectory models on field data.\n\u2022 Deliverables & Validation Gate (M6): Comprehensive Mid-Term Clinical Validation Report evaluating screening accuracy, false-positive rates, and user adoption. The solution will be fully ready for independent clinical validation by Month 6.\n\u2022 Dependencies: Timely hardware procurement and district health society permissions.\n\n\u2022 Phase 3: Multi-District Scale & 108 Emergency Referral Integration (Months 7\u20139)\n\u2022 M7: Expand to three additional high-burden districts: Tinsukia, Dhubri, and Sonitpur, onboarding 2,000 ASHAs and 480 ANMs.\n\u2022 M8: Implement bidirectional REST APIs with GVK EMRI 108/102 Mrityunjoy CAD and FRU obstetric ICU bed dashboards.\n\u2022 M9: Activate automated bilingual Assamese/Bengali voice and SMS maternal advisory engine.\n\u2022 Deliverables: 5-District Operational Grid, Automated 108 Emergency Gateway, Multilingual Patient Notification Engine.\n\u2022 Dependencies: GVK EMRI CAD API access and C-DAC SMS gateway provisioning.\n\n\u2022 Phase 4: ABDM Interoperability, CERT-In Audit & Institutional Handover (Months 10\u201312)\n\u2022 M10: Finalize two-way ABDM FHIR R4 sync with national e-Kavach / ANMOL and the RCH portal.\n\u2022 M11: Complete mandatory third-party CERT-In cybersecurity audit (VAPT). Conduct statewide health system impact workshop.\n\u2022 M12: Transition software repositories, CI/CD pipelines, cryptographic keys, and administrative control to NHM Assam IT Cell.\n\u2022 Deliverables: CERT-In Security Certificate, ABDM Compliance Badges, Multi-Centric Impact Study, Final Handover Charter."
