    "content": "(Word Count: 462 words / Limit: 500 words)\n\nData Categories, Formats & Ingestion Pipeline\nTo develop, calibrate, and validate MatriDrishti without violating patient privacy or making unconfirmed access assumptions, the platform utilizes four structured data streams:\n\n1. Physiological Telemetry & Vital Signs:\n\u2022 Parameters: Systolic Blood Pressure (SBP, mmHg), Diastolic Blood Pressure (DBP, mmHg), Pulse Rate (BPM), and derived Mean Arterial Pressure (MAP = \\frac{2\\cdot DBP + SBP}{3}).\n\u2022 Format: Structured JSON payloads conforming to IEEE 11073-10407 health device communication standards, ingested directly via BLE GATT or on-device OCR.\n2. Point-of-Care Diagnostic Urine Protein:\n\u2022 Parameters: Proteinuria grading (Negative, Trace, 1+ [30 mg/dL], 2+ [100 mg/dL], 3+ [300 mg/dL], 4+ [\\ge1000 mg/dL]).\n\u2022 Format: RGB colorimetric values and categorical string enums logged from optical test strip scanning.\n3. Maternal Longitudinal Clinical Profile:\n\u2022 Parameters: Gestational age (weeks/days based on Last Menstrual Period / early dating ultrasound), maternal age, parity, previous history of pre-eclampsia/eclampsia, chronic hypertension, pre-gestational diabetes, and baseline Body Mass Index (BMI).\n\u2022 Format: HL7 FHIR R4 JSON resources (Observation, Condition, Encounter, CarePlan).\n4. Geospatial & Facility Administrative Metadata:\n\u2022 Parameters: Village/tea estate/char hamlet coordinates (WGS84 lat/long), catchment polygon boundaries, road network navigability graphs, and nearest Health Facility Registry (HFR) codes for Sub-Centres, PHCs, FRUs, and District Hospitals.\n\u2022 Format: GeoJSON and PostGIS spatial geometry layers.\n\nProcessing, Annotation & Outlier Rejection Protocols\n\u2022 Signal Quality & Anomaly Filtering: Serial blood pressure readings undergo automated z-score outlier detection and Kalman filtering to reject physiological movement artifacts (e.g., patient talking or cuff slippage during measurement).\n\u2022 Time-Series Normalization: Longitudinal MAP values are resampled and normalized against gestational age milestones (MAP_{12\\text{w}}, MAP_{16\\text{w}}, MAP_{20\\text{w}}, MAP_{24\\text{w}}), computing velocity derivatives:\n  $\\frac{d(MAP)}{dt} \\approx \\frac{MAP_{t_2} - MAP_{t_1}}{t_2 - t_1}$\n\nZero Unconfirmed Access Assumption & Data Governance\n\u2022 No Unconfirmed Retrospective Access Assumed: Initial development and algorithm benchmarking do not rely on unconfirmed access to private state patient registries. Base model architectures are trained using anonymized, open-access international maternal hemodynamic datasets (e.g., PhysioNet, MIMIC-III, and UK Biobank cohorts).\n\u2022 Synthetic Generative Bootstrapping: To simulate Assam-specific epidemiological distributions prior to field rollout, the team utilizes Gaussian Copula generative algorithms to create 10,000 synthetic maternal profiles reflecting Upper Assam tea estate and riverine char demographic traits (high anemia prevalence, young maternal age, high parity).\n\u2022 Prospective Field Collection Under Ethics Approval: Real-world training data is collected strictly prospectively during Phase 2 field pilots across Dibrugarh and Barpeta under formal Institutional Ethics Committee (IEC) approval from AMCH Dibrugarh and informed digital consent from participating pregnant women, adhering strictly to the Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023."
